README.md:157:- Every trade supports: entry/exit times, R:R ratio, planned risk, MAE/MFE, exit reason, magic number, entry legs, balance after, tags, chart link, screenshots, and a rich text journal
README.md:167:Content autosaves 1.5 seconds after the last keystroke with a live Saving / Saved indicator. Templates let you define a document structure once and auto-apply it whenever you open a new journal for a specific trade type.
README.md:171:A dedicated strategy library separate from the journal. Document each setup you trade — its rules, entry triggers, exit criteria, timeframes, and instruments — then link individual trades to it from the journal editor or the trade quick-view panel.
README.md:197:**R-Multiples** — R-multiple histogram using average loss as 1R. Average R per trade, expectancy in R units, and symbol breakdown.
README.md:247:Report builder with date range, ticker, tag, and status filters. Toggle individual sections on or off — cover page, performance summary, daily breakdown, trade history, journal entries. Live preview before generating. The PDF renders entirely in the browser — no data is transmitted anywhere.
README.md:272:Shortcuts are disabled while typing in any input field or the journal editor.
README.md:316:you trust it with a real journal. It is **not** a seed script — nothing runs it
README.md:379:**Journal editor.** Built on TipTap with ProseMirror. Documents stored as TipTap JSON in the `journalEntry` TEXT column. Legacy plain-text entries render as plain paragraphs. Autosave debounces 1.5 seconds and patches the in-memory trade immediately so navigation never shows stale content.
README.md:383:**Template system.** Templates stored as TipTap JSON with a scope string (`all`, `option`, `stock`, `future`). Auto-apply runs when the editor opens an empty journal — applies silently if exactly one template matches.
README.md:466:- Playbook linking from journal editor and trade panel
README.md:522:<sub>Previously released as Tradello (v1.0.0 – v2.3.0). Renamed to better reflect its purpose — turning your journal into your edge.</sub>
